hose factory workers  are gonna lose jobs there are going to  be some of those hundred and forty  thousand steel production workers that  will benefit there'll be lots more of  the five million steel workers that use  them as inputs that are going to suffer  we need to start telling the American  people the truth about what's happening  in big factory jobs and the analog is  agriculture in nineteen hundred more  than forty percent of Americans worked  on farms a hundred years later less than  two percent and yet we produce more  stuff that's what's happening in  industrial factory jobs right now we  have rapidly declining numbers of people  working in industrial jobs but we have  more total output we need to start  developing our technology it's very  clear to all of us listening how much  you love your state and how much you're  against this proposal but back to John's  original question what can you do what  are you going to do about  yeah I mean I'm gonna talk to you and  I'm going to talk to the American people  because the president has the power to  do this under current law it's stupid  policy but he has the authority there's  a there's a big fight happening inside  the administration right now because  most senior people in the White House  know that this is a really dumb policy  and the American people have forgotten  workers of even the Rust Belt states  they don't want to be drafted and be  casualties in a stupid trade war and so  there are a bunch of people inside the  administration trying to talk the  president out of this but you can see  the mixed messages coming out of the  administration when we say we're doing  this to target China and you know who  loses most Canada one of our fundamental  partners there are main in there the  main exporter of steel to the US senator  you talk about the organization inside  the White House you used to repair  organizations for a living assess the  organization inside the White House  right now so it's it's a tough place to  work and there are a lot of really good  people there and the President does  deserve credit for a lot of good people  he's put in this administration somebody  like Don Magan who's helping him pick  judges doing a phenomenal job a lot of  the regular triage and a lot of them are  leaving it's it's a chaotic place Gail  I'm not gonna argue with you about that  and ultimately this White House is a  reflection of this president and he said  that he likes chaos I don't think that's  really a great way to run an  organization but I saved most of my  counsel on that topic for the president  in private we actually have a  surprisingly good relationship we  wrestle a lot in private before I'm out  here criticizing him in public but in  the trade war that we're talking about  today it's gonna hurt Americans it's  gonna hurt American families and it's  gonna cost us jobs and I hope the  president walks back from the brink okay  see if he's listening to you thank you  very much senators house for taking your  time this morning
 

